The fake cvs program prints what "cvs diff" prints.  The program removes the details of each
difference, keeping only the file name, and makes each file name absolute.

The replacer for "cvs diff: cannot find FILE" inserts the directory without a "/" after it, so the
directory and the file name run together.  The goal file records the current (wrong) behavior; the
line should end with "${HOME}/mod/gone.txt".

Bug report: https://github.com/plume-lib/multi-version-control/issues/615
